cuems-editor (0.1.1-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Coordinated xml-refactor landing (cuems-utils feature 016): every CUEMS
    repository moves to its own next stable minor. This entry folds the
    never-shipped 0.1.0rc1-4 entry below; 0.1.0rc1-4 .. -7 were since
    released from debian/bookworm without this content, so those numbers
    stay with the builds that shipped under them. Version sites agree on
    0.1.1 (pyproject.toml, cuemseditor.__version__).
  * Depends: cuems-common (>= 1.3.1~), was (>= 1.0.0), a floor older than
    the node-identity contract.
  * Reconciled with the release line origin/debian/bookworm at 69d749e
    (0.1.0rc1-7), merged with its history (origin/rc1 is inside it; no
    cherry-pick): the released entries 0.1.0rc1-4 .. -7 follow verbatim.
    Absorbed: the pixel size, file size and MD5 of each media file stored at
    upload and written on every save, new and duplicate included (869fat84r,
    -4); the media check at open, before the load and after a save, its
    media_check_report, the save-time re-measurement and the video-index
    rebuild (-4), re-implemented on CuemsScript objects, one comparison
    feeding both this report and the load report's media_repairs, never
    gating a save; the save gate for media cues without a usable media block
    or naming a file the library never saw (869fej07m, -5), on the current
    wire (Cue with class audio|video); no /usr/lib/cuems/CACHEDIR.TAG (-6);
    media name collisions with trashed or stray files (-7); node adoption
    over the WebSocket (already in this line).
  * A loaded but stopped project (the engine's project_status "loaded") is
    not a show running: the media check no longer skips it.
  * A 0.1.0rc1-4 behaviour that did not survive: a save into a directory the
    editor cannot create files in no longer falls back to writing in place.
    CuemsScript.save writes atomically and raises; reported to cuems-utils.
  * stop_project (cuems-engine rc6-5): the editor sends no target and clears
    a leftover one. Saving such a cue needs cuems-utils at or after the
    re-cut of its xml-refactor-merge-candidate (script.xsd carries the value
    from 0.1.0rc17); until then its tests are strict expected failures.
  * The controller, the engine and the frontend upgrade together; mixed
    versions are not supported.
  * 001-cuems-utils-migration: move onto the public cuemsutils surface.
    cuemsutils 0.1.0rc16 no longer ships cuemsutils.create_script, so the
    0.1.0rc1-3 editor died at import against it. Scripts now load and save
    through CuemsScript (load_with_report / from_json / save); the node
    split is cuemsutils.tools.NodeList.partition_by_adoption (cuems-utils
    013, 6213b16); initial_template is the library's generated example.
  * debian/control: bound cuems-utils on both sides,
    cuems-utils (>= 0.1.1), cuems-utils (<< 0.1.2~) since cuems-utils 016.
    0.1.2 deletes the deprecated surface; the pair matches cuems-nodeconf.
  * cuems-editor-repair-durations no longer writes project scripts. It
    corrects the database and lists the projects that need a save in the
    editor.
  * Not a controller release on its own: the project frame now carries
    Cue / CueOutput with class (cuems-utils 013), which a pre-05
    cuems-frontend mis-reads. Ships with the coordinated tag.

 -- Adrià Masip <adria@stagelab.coop>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200

cuems-editor (0.1.0rc1-7) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Merge rc1 into debian/bookworm.
  * Node adoption over the editor WebSocket (869ebkkme, PR #7): nodelist_get
    with uuid validation, nodelist_modify relayed to the engine, map changes
    pushed to every client, the engine's liveness view relayed as
    node_status (load diagnosis verbatim); nodeconf_available no longer
    cached. Adopting needs an engine with the nodelist_modify hop and a
    running cuems-nodeconf; against an older engine the request errors.
    Same code as the 0.1.0rc1-5+nodeadopt2 test-rig builds.
  * Media library (PR #10): uploading a file named like a media in the
    trash no longer fails with "UNIQUE constraint failed: media.unix_name";
    it gets the versioned name <base>-NNN<ext>, as any duplicate does.
    Delete and restore keep the media's unix_name (cues reference media by
    filename): an untracked file already in the trash is moved aside, an
    untracked live file in media/ refuses the restore with a clear error,
    and both undo their own moves on rollback.
  * The 869fej07m save gate is unchanged (already shipped since 0.1.0rc1-5;
    rc1 got its back-port, PR #8). No new cuems-utils floor (>= 0.1.0rc15).

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Fri, 09 Oct 2026 14:14:49 +0200

cuems-editor (0.1.0rc1-6) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * packaging: stop shipping /usr/lib/cuems/CACHEDIR.TAG. The 0.1.0rc1-5
    build picked it up from virtualenv and cuems-utils 0.1.0rc16 ships the
    same path, so installing utils after the editor failed with "trying to
    overwrite" unless forced. It is venv infrastructure like pyvenv.cfg
    (already stripped); nothing reads it at runtime.
  * No code change from 0.1.0rc1-5.

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Fri, 09 Oct 2026 12:41:21 +0200

cuems-editor (0.1.0rc1-5) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Save gate (869fej07m): new / update refuse a project in which an audio
    or video cue arrives without a usable media block (no Media, null, an
    empty object, no or empty file_name, no id) or names a file the library
    has never seen, before anything is written - project row, ProjectMedia
    rows and the XML stay untouched. A file in the media trash still passes
    (it can be restored). The WS error carries the plain message naming the
    cue instead of "<class 'KeyError'> 'file_name'". Closes the path by
    which a save from the edit page silently emptied a cue's <Media/>.
    No new cuems-utils floor (>= 0.1.0rc15 stays; rc16 adds the matching
    guards in the library itself).

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 21:15:57 +0200

cuems-editor (0.1.0rc1-4) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Merge rc1 into debian/bookworm (869fat84r): store each media file's
    pixel size (video), size and MD5 at upload and write them into every
    cue of a project on save (new, update, duplicate); legacy rows are
    measured once at save, never hashed. At load and save, check the
    project's media against the library and send a media_check_report to
    the project's sessions; the project file is never rewritten at load.
  * debian/control: require cuems-utils (>= 0.1.0rc15). An older utils
    schema rejects every save of a project with a video cue.

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Tue, 06 Oct 2026 20:18:57 +0200

cuems-editor (0.1.0rc1-3) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Merge rc1 into debian/bookworm (43 commits since 0.1.0rc1-2, 2026-03-
    10).
  * FIX: the 0.1.0rc1-1/-2 debs were cut from a base predating 80c7642
    (2026-02-05) and still did 'from cuemsutils.daemon import
    run_daemon'. cuemsutils dropped that module, so against cuems-utils
    0.1.0rc14 the service died at import with ModuleNotFoundError and
    restart-looped. The merged rc1 source uses foreground mode under
    systemd instead.
  * debian/control: require cuems-utils (>= 0.1.0rc10), matching the
    lockstep requirement pyproject.toml has declared since 8da2570. The
    old (>= 0.1.0rc4) floor permitted exactly the editor/utils version
    skew that caused the breakage above.
  * Brings in save-time FadeCue duration validation and the CUE_TYPES
    FadeCue dangling-target fix.

